description:
It's really just a matter of taste but you could protect the linkage of source-file level helpers by enclosing them in an anonymous namespace (rather than using static). e.g.

namespace {

int helper() {
   // etc
}

}

You can add the Rcpp::interfaces attribute to make your exported functions directly available to C++ clients:

// [[Rcpp::interfaces(r, cpp)]]

This will generate inst/include/scrypt.h with the right C++ shims exposed.
